            <ArticleTitle>Discovery of non-LBD inhibitor for androgen receptor by structure-guide design.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3887-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2013.04.065</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(13)00546-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this study, we synthesized the BF-3 binding small molecules, a series of pyridazinone-based compounds, as a novel class of non-LBP antiandrogens for treating prostate cancer by inhibiting androgen receptor. The new class compound was discovered to inhibitor the viability of AR-dependent human prostate LNCap cells and AR activity combining with the computational method. It showed a good physicochemical and PK property.</AbstractText>
